ENGLISH VERSION (courtesy translation)
=========================================================================

1. Permission granted

   You may view and read the Repository, online on GitHub, for personal
   purposes: reading, information, or evaluating the work.

   You may also install and update Bonk from the repositories and scripts
   published at https://packages.bonk-os.app, with the public key published
   there, as its instructions describe. Packages installed this way are
   governed by the license of the Bonk software (section 6).

2. What is prohibited

   Without prior written permission from Bonk, you may not:

   a) copy, reproduce or download the Repository, in whole or in part, beyond
      what is strictly necessary to read it;
   b) use the Repository: run it, build it, deploy it, host it, put it online,
      integrate it into another project or derive a service from it;
   c) modify, adapt, translate or create a derivative work of the Repository;
   d) distribute, publish, communicate to the public, lend, rent, sell or
      sublicense the Repository, in whole or in part;
   e) reuse the name, visual identity, texts, structure or design of the
      Repository for another site or product, or create confusion with Bonk,
      bonk-os.app or packages.bonk-os.app;
   f) remove or alter copyright and ownership notices.

   Making a copy available to others is not permitted, even free of charge.

3. GitHub terms of service

   The rights that GitHub's terms of service grant to users of the platform
   (viewing, copying within GitHub to the extent those terms require) remain
   only to that extent. They give no right to use the Repository outside
   GitHub.

4. Vulnerability research

   Good-faith security research within the scope and rules published at
   https://security.bonk-os.app is not a violation of this license.

5. Third-party components

   The Repository contains or uses components that do not belong to Bonk
   (libraries, trademarks, logos). They remain subject to their own licenses
   and owners; this license neither grants nor removes any right on them.

6. The Bonk software

   The Bonk software (https://github.com/FantasmaGlad/Bonk) is a separate
   project released under its own license (MIT). This license does not apply
   to it, and its license does not apply to this Repository.

7. Contributions

   A contribution is accepted only with Bonk's written agreement, which sets
   its terms, including the assignment of rights in the contribution.

8. No warranty

   The Repository is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express
   or implied. Bonk is not liable for any damage resulting from its reading or
   from unauthorized use.

9. Termination

   Any violation of this license immediately ends the right to view granted in
   section 1, without prejudice to other remedies.

10. Governing law

    This license is governed by French law.

11. Permission

    For any other use, write to security@bonk-os.app describing the intended
    use. A permission is valid only if written.
